# Round 1 review-gate findings: negative controls

Working tree starts from 8cdcc936. Each control breaks one invariant, runs the
test that pins it, and is then reverted before the green run.

## Finding 1 (docs/lessons/1986-relay-wire-assumptions.md): ledger records a correction the diff lacks

$ node scripts/lessons-ledger-gate.mjs
lessons ledger ok

Format was never the defect: docs/lessons/ is the active ledger on origin/main (226 entries),
docs/lessons.md does not exist there, and this gate passes the entry. The real defect was the
entry asserting a wrong-request-index correction and a trailing-newline mismatch that the diff
does not contain. A probe measured the request layout of a handoff run:

$ probe of stub requests in a handoff run
status pass requests 3
0 nmsg 2 lastRole user roles system,user
1 nmsg 2 lastRole user roles system,user
2 nmsg 4 lastRole tool roles system,user,assistant,tool

The executor request is index 2, not 1, and no trailing-newline assertion exists in the
branch. The entry is rewritten to claim only what the branch supports.

